uthorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"06b09c7248296e5d458042d6e46696aba8efb42e61896a7673cfb1053ea3fcb7","event_uuid":"421efb15-e2a0-4f02-97f2-344231d4a31e","position":{"commit_sha":"3904ee5d95f80303b7a7fe36a15f85ea248d29b7","position":"1788540250018171119-421efb15-e2a0-4f02-97f2-344231d4a31e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788538192602626001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aab4de1e-e0f3-4219-9971-0c70f625c251","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"90c7-c465-4037-42d5"},{"link_uuid":"421efb15-e2a0-4f02-97f2-344231d4a31e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"512b-78ab-e391-4fb1"}],"description":"## Goal\n\nPrevent a repeat of incident `90c7-c465-4037-42d5` (the scanner-integration hard lock): a NEW blocking CI check (`scanner-integration`) was wired directly into the required Verified vote aggregate in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, failed on every full-route change, and produced a fleet-wide CI lock that only a human force-submit could break. Establish a durable policy — as an Accepted ADR plus lean agent guidance — that a new gate may only join the required \"hot path\" AFTER it has demonstrated a passing CI run running independently (advisory / non-blocking) on `main`.\n\n## Policy (the decision to record)\n\n- Before any new check is added to — or promoted into — the required Verified vote aggregate (the \"hot path\") in `.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml`, it MUST first run as an ADVISORY (non-voting, non-blocking) job and show at least one passing CI run on `main` independent of the hot path.\n- Only after that independent green run may a separate, subsequent change promote it into the vote aggregate's blocking `needs`/route conditions.\n- SCOPE: this applies ONLY to modifications of `.github/workflows/**` that add or promote a REQUIRED gate into the Verified vote aggregate. It does NOT apply to ordinary test-suite additions (new tests under `tests/` run by the existing suite are unaffected).\n- Rationale: a gate wired straight into the aggregate that fails self-referentially locks the fleet, because the fix itself is full-route and cannot earn Verified +1 — exactly what happened in 90c7. Sibling precedent: ADR 0110 (change shape enters the floor as an advisory first).\n\n## Scope / Deliverables\n\n- `docs/adr/0114-<slug>.md`: NEW ADR, `Status: Accepted`, dated, with Context (cite incident 90c7 and the `gerrit-verify.yaml` vote aggregate self-lock), Decision (advisory-first + independent passing run before hot-path promotion; scope limited to GHA workflow gate additions; excludes test-suite additions), and Consequences.\n- `docs/adr/README.md`: regenerate the ADR index to include 0114 via `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` (do NOT hand-edit the generated index).\n- `AGENTS.md`: add a ONE-LINE pointer to ADR 0114 in the Git-workflow / CI section (keep the file lean per its own policy; do not restate the ADR).\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n1. ADR number is 0114 (main's highest is 0113). If a concurrent change takes 0114, use the next free integer and rerun the generator.\n2. The ADR index in `docs/adr/README.md` is GENERATED; edit it only via `scripts/gen_adr_index.py`, then validate with `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` and `scripts/check_docs_index.py`.\n3. AGENTS.md guidance is a lean pointer only (the repo's AGENTS.md policy forbids restating documented content); the authoritative text lives in the ADR.\n4. This is a docs/guidance change: no source or workflow behavior is modified (the policy is process guidance, not a new gate).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0114-<slug>.md` exists with `**Status:** Accepted`, a date, and Context/Decision/Consequences sections; Context cites incident `90c7` and the `gerrit-verify.yaml` Verified vote aggregate; Decision states advisory-first + an independent passing CI run before hot-path promotion.\n- [ ] The Decision explicitly scopes the rule to `.github/workflows/**` changes that add/promote a REQUIRED gate into the Verified vote aggregate, and explicitly EXCLUDES ordinary test-suite additions.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/README.md` lists ADR 0114, produced by re-running `scripts/gen_adr_index.py` (not hand-edited).\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` contains a single-line pointer to ADR 0114 in the CI/Git-workflow guidance.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_docs_index.py` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` passes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python scripts/check_docs_index.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Do NOT modify `.github/workflows/**` or add/change any actual CI gate; this ticket only records the policy and guidance.\n- Do NOT restate ADR content in AGENTS.md beyond a one-line pointer.\n- Do NOT re-add the reverted scanner-integration work (that redo is tracked under `b973`).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/adr/0114-advisory-gate-before-hot-path.md","reason":"New Accepted ADR recording the advisory-first / independent-passing-run-before-hot-path-promotion policy; cite incident 90c7 and the gerrit-verify.yaml vote aggregate."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Regenerate the ADR index (via scripts/gen_adr_index.py) to include ADR 0114; do not hand-edit."},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0114","reason":"ADR-number registry marker created by scripts/gen_adr_index.py when reserving number 0114; generator-owned, committed alongside the index regeneration."},{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"Add a one-line pointer to ADR 0114 in the CI/Git-workflow guidance; keep lean, no restated content."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","512b-78ab-e391-4fb1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5802ce7d-1ec1-4693-a53e-2ce57144c774","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"374a-780a-390e-4c39","ticket_type":"task","title":"ADR + agent guidance: new CI gates must pass independently before joining the Verified hot path","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1c308640-45b7-4d74-bc82-b298f45704a6","1d54e480-e79f-4c43-87cd-701ae9578a40","aab4de1e-e0f3-4219-9971-0c70f625c251","fd721a38-7fad-44b9-a5c2-731f144328f4","5802ce7d-1ec1-4693-a53e-2ce57144c774","c6099e95-3856-4be1-9899-87786d581df4","3aabeabc-4254-4f63-96c2-0920f49b9191","421efb15-e2a0-4f02-97f2-344231d4a31e"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788540250018171120,"uuid":"3b264cb0-1c8f-48d1-b2b5-224a32207146"}